# BNB Smart Chain RPC (mainnet chain id 56)
NEXT_PUBLIC_BSC_RPC_URL=https://bsc-dataseed.binance.org/
# BSC testnet (chain id 97)
NEXT_PUBLIC_BSC_TESTNET_RPC_URL=https://data-seed-prebsc-1-s1.binance.org:8545/

# Which BNB Chain deployment to read and settle against: 56 (mainnet) or 97 (testnet).
# Defaults to 56. Contract addresses live in lib/chain/addresses.ts, not here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID=56

# Public base URL used in the A2A agent card + API docs.
#
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. This value is stamped into /.well-known/agent.json,
# into every documented example and into metadataBase, so a machine caller
# resolves Bazar through it. If it is unset, lib/constants.ts falls back to the
# platform-reported host (VERCEL_URL, which only Vercel sets) and then to
# http://localhost:3000 - which is a broken discovery URL, not a default. Any
# non-Vercel deployment (Docker, a plain Node server) MUST set it, as must any
# custom domain on Vercel. A production build that falls through logs a warning
# on boot.
#
# Leave it commented out for local development only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-deployment.example

# --- Log-reading RPC (optional, but read this before you file a bug) ---------
#
# The Binance dataseed hosts above answer eth_call fine but REFUSE eth_getLogs
# entirely - "Request exceeds defined limit." for every range, down to a fifty
# block window. Measured 2026-08-28 across bsc-dataseed.binance.org, defibit,
# ninicoin, data-seed-prebsc-* and bsc-testnet-dataseed.bnbchain.org. That is
# not a range cap chunking can work around, so lib/chain/client.ts keeps a
# SECOND client per chain purely for logs, and any job listing scoped to a
# wallet address (readJobsForClient) reads through it.
#
# Unset, it defaults to PublicNode, the only public host that served logs for
# these contracts: ~2,000-block ranges on mainnet, ~50,000 on testnet, and a
# large fraction of consecutive requests dropped. Scans are chunked, retried
# and allowed to return a partial answer because of exactly that. Point these
# at a paid endpoint to remove both the range cap and the failures.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BSC_LOGS_RPC_URL=https://bsc-rpc.publicnode.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BSC_TESTNET_LOGS_RPC_URL=https://bsc-testnet-rpc.publicnode.com
